     which is set at stepper.go:284 (MonthlyLivingExpenses * multiplier *
     CumulativeInflation) BEFORE floorAdjustedLiving (stepper.go:297-298,326)
     computes the separate adjustedLivingExpenses. st.CurrentLivingExpenses is
     never overwritten by floorAdjustedLiving's output. CONFIRMED: figure is
     genuinely pre-floor and pre-guardrail-multiplier, as documented.
   - "from year N" wording precision: LowestPlannedLivingReal reports the
     first month attaining the GLOBAL minimum over the whole horizon, not
     necessarily a phase start; on a non-monotonic custom schedule spending
     could rise back above the floor after year N while the wording implies
     an ongoing state. OBSERVATION only (wording, not a wrong figure) per
     task instructions — Amount/Year/Phase are still exactly correct.

